  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Through fictional and historical narratives, Descendant traces a personal southern lineage that begins with Gibson, an African brought to Jamestown, Virginia, in the 1600's, and stretches twelve generations and 400 years into the present."--Artist's statement.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book comprised of six niches or recesses, formed by the space between half-arched wooden panels.  Wooden text panel slides into each niche. The panels contain text on recto and verso and can be partially removed, but are held to the whole by braided twine. The niches are covered and hinged (top, bottom, and one side) with goat parchment. With stud and ring clasp, the ring on one end of braided twine that passes through the middle of the wooden panels and prohibits complete removal of any text panel.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 20 copies, signed by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
